Release Tracker — Java-to-Python Migration Gap Analysis & Fix Plan

1. Objective

The Release Tracker Java application is the working and approved reference implementation.

The Python application is the migrated implementation and currently has multiple functional gaps in both the frontend and backend.

The objective of this task is:

Compare the Java implementation and the Python implementation feature-by-feature, page-by-page, API-by-API, and fix the Python application so that it behaves the same as the Java application.

The Java application’s existing business logic, UI behavior, data flow, API behavior, database behavior, filtering, asynchronous processing, and validations must be treated as the source of truth.

Critical Rule

This is a migration correction task, not a redesign or feature-development task.

Do NOT introduce new business logic unless it is required to reproduce the existing Java behavior.

Do NOT simplify, redesign, remove, or reinterpret existing Java logic.

The expected difference is primarily:

* Java → Python backend implementation
* Existing React/TypeScript frontend behavior must remain equivalent
* Existing database behavior must remain equivalent
* Existing API inputs/outputs must remain equivalent
* Existing asynchronous/parallel behavior must remain equivalent

